# High Tide reads the land type, not the name (its rulings: "any land with the land type Island"; CR 305.6), and its
# additional {U} comes at once, even in the middle of paying a cost (CR 605.4a). Turn 7: with High Tide resolved, Bot1
# casts Lord of Atlantis ({U}{U}) and taps one Island while paying: the Island's {U} and High Tide's pay the whole cost,
# so Tropical Island, the other source of {U}, stays untapped. Tapped later for {G}, Tropical Island, an Island Forest,
# still adds the additional {U}, while a Forest adds nothing more.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
High Tide
Tropical Island
Forest
Lord of Atlantis
Island
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Tropical Island.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.High Tide.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Lord of Atlantis.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
? Stack = Lord of Atlantis
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Tropical Island.Activate(Ability: {G})
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Mana = {U}{G}
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {U}{G}{G}

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = High Tide
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Island; Island; Lord of Atlantis; Tropical Island
